 "sentences": [
  "Now, regarding your day-to-day tasks, I want to emphasize the importance of clear and concise coding practices.",
  "One of the standards we uphold in our team is the consistent use of annotations for methods.",
  "It's a simple yet effective way to enhance code readability and maintainability.",
  "So, moving forward, I'd like you to ensure that all your methods are appropriately annotated.",
  "Not at this stage, Lucas.",
  "Simply ensuring that your code is well-annotated will be a great start.",
  "Of course, if you have any questions or encounter any challenges, please don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "Firstly, I want you to get into the habit of always including try statements in your methods.",
  "This will help with error handling and ensure that your code is more robust.",
  "Proper documentation is crucial for code maintainability and collaboration.",
  "These practices will not only improve your coding skills but also ensure that your code aligns with industry standards and best practices.",
  "Conflict resolution is an important aspect of any healthy work environment.",
  "It's all about fostering an environment where everyone feels heard and respected, and any issues can be discussed openly without fear of escalation.",
  "Going forward, we want you to start function argument names with 'a_'.",
  "Consistency is key, and it's the little things that add up to make our code base robust and maintainable.",
  "Having those kinds of tools at our disposal can really enhance our capabilities and reduce the time spent on certain tasks.",
  "Let's make sure to include that in our proposal."
 ],
 "admitted": 17,
